<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="style.css">
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="styleHeader.css">
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="styleFooter.css">
    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="Logo.svg">
    <title>Inventory</title>
</head>
<body>
    <header>
        <%- include('header'); %>
    </header>
    <main>
        <div class="firstIndexPart">
            <h3>Welcome...</h3>
            <p>This page is an inventory app in which you will have to main items (author and book) in which you can add a new instance of those items.
                You can also erase every item that you add and also update it in case you write wrong information.
                Also you can create different categories in base of common things that your items have such as the genre of the book or the author. Just like the
                items you can erase categories and update them in case you put wrong information. <br>
                <span>ENJOY THE PAGE.</span>
            </p>
        </div>
        <div class="secondIndexPart">
            <h2>How to use the page</h2>
            <p>To use this page is really simple, you just have to hover the mouse on the section of "categories" or "items" to check all the items
                or the categories you already have. You can also click on the "Add book/category/author" texts to add what you want. Also you can click on 
                the "inventory" title to return to this page. Finally, do not forget that you can update and create new items and categories. <br>
                <span>Lets try to view all the books we have by just clicking the button</span>
            </p>
            <button>View books</button>
            <img src="Logo.svg" alt="The_Logo_Face" class="theLogoFace">
            <img src="Hand.svg" alt="The_Logo_Hand" class="theLogoHand">
        </div>
    </main>
    <footer>
        <%- include('footer') %>
    </footer>
</body>
</html>